\label{pr:lie}
	Let $\mathfrak g$ be the algebra from \cref{def}.
	Then:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item $\mathfrak g$ is a Lie algebra.
		\item $\mathfrak g$ is generated by $x_1$ and $y_1$ and is $5$-step nilpotent.
		\item The lower central series of $\mathfrak g$ is $\mathfrak g^k := \bigoplus_{j=k}^5 \mathfrak g_j$. In particular, $\mathfrak g = \langle x_1, y_1 \rangle \oplus [\mathfrak g, \mathfrak g]$.
	\end{enumerate}
